# API rules — {{ project_name }}

## Design
- Validate inputs at the boundary; fail with clear errors
- Never trust client-provided IDs, roles, or amounts for authorisation
- Keep handlers thin — business logic in services

## Security
- Auth check before sensitive reads/writes
- Rate-limit or guard public endpoints where appropriate
- Log errors without leaking secrets or PII

## Backend: {{ backend }}
- Document env vars in `.env.example`
- Use migrations for schema changes
- Test happy path and common failure modes

## Verification
- Run `{{ commands.test }}` after API changes
- Add or update tests for new endpoints and edge cases
